// The lifter (export): reads the TASTy of Models compiled against the framework and writes the Umpire
// IR. The TASTy inspector's compiler must be at least as new as the one that compiled the Models.
// Its IR classes are generated by the gate (model/temporal/check); the JDK and scala-cli come from
// mise.toml. It names no system and has no system's API on its classpath: a system's lifter is built
// from this directory and the system's half, this one first (Temporal's: `scala-cli <command>
// model/framework/export model/temporal/export`), which adds its API classes, the classes a
// realization's messages are read from.
//> using scala 3.9.0
//> using file ../../OutputPaths.scala
//> using file ../lint
//> using file ../inspect
//> using file ../reify/body
//> using file ../dsl
//> using file ../realize
//> using options -Werror -deprecation -feature -unchecked -Wunused:all -Wvalue-discard -Wnonunit-statement -Wsafe-init -Wimplausible-patterns -language:strictEquality
//> using dep org.scala-lang::scala3-tasty-inspector:3.9.0
//> using dep com.thesamet.scalapb::scalapb-runtime:0.11.20
//> using dep com.thesamet.scalapb::scalapb-runtime-grpc:0.11.20
//> using dep com.thesamet.scalapb::scalapb-json4s:0.12.2
//> using jar ../../build/ir-scalapb.jar
// The tests build the fixtures under testdata with scala-cli and run the lifter as its own JVM,
// through the checks' one place for running a tool. scala-cli has no directive that adds a source to
// the test scope only, so the file is compiled beside the lifter, which uses only its `Scratch`.
//> using file ../check/Tools.scala
// The suites keep their scratch only when they fail (Retaining.test.scala).
//> using file ../check/Retaining.test.scala
//> using test.dep org.scalameta::munit:1.2.0
// The tests build fixtures and lift in-process, three builds and three lifts at a time
// (ModelBuild.test.scala, InProcess.test.scala); a bounded heap keeps the suite inside the memory
// of a shared machine, and the lifter's own runs fit it as well.
//> using javaOpt -Xmx3g
// The fixtures under testdata are their own builds, and some must not compile; the tests copy them
// out and build each apart.
//> using exclude testdata
